  "vulnerabilities": [
    {
      "id": "GHSA-29mw-wpgm-hmr9",
      "references": [
        {
          "id": "CVE-2020-28500",
          "source": {}
        }
      ],
      "ratings": [
        {
          "score": 5.3,
          "severity": "medium",
          "method": "CVSSv3",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) in lodash",
      "detail": "All versions of package lodash prior to 4.17.21 are vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) via the `toNumber`, `trim` and `trimEnd` functions. \n\nSteps to reproduce (provided by reporter Liyuan Chen):\n```js\nvar lo = require('lodash');\n\nfunction build_blank(n) {\n    var ret = \"1\"\n    for (var i = 0; i \u003c n; i++) {\n        ret += \" \"\n    }\n    return ret + \"1\";\n}\nvar s = build_blank(50000) var time0 = Date.now();\nlo.trim(s) \nvar time_cost0 = Date.now() - time0;\nconsole.log(\"time_cost0: \" + time_cost0);\nvar time1 = Date.now();\nlo.toNumber(s) var time_cost1 = Date.now() - time1;\nconsole.log(\"time_cost1: \" + time_cost1);\nvar time2 = Date.now();\nlo.trimEnd(s);\nvar time_cost2 = Date.now() - time2;\nconsole.log(\"time_cost2: \" + time_cost2);\n```",
      "advisories": [
        {
          "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-28500"
        }
      ],
      "published": "2022-01-06T20:30:46Z",
      "updated": "2025-09-29T21:12:31Z",
      "credits": {
        "organizations": []
      },
      "affects": [
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-es"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash.trimend"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash.trim"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:gem/lodash-rails"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm",
      "references": [
        {
          "id": "CVE-2021-23337",
          "source": {}
        }
      ],
      "ratings": [
        {
          "score": 7.2,
          "severity": "high",
          "method": "CVSSv3",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Command Injection in lodash",
      "detail": "`lodash` versions prior to 4.17.21 are vulnerable to Command Injection via the template function.",
      "advisories": [
        {
          "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-23337"
        }
      ],
      "published": "2021-05-06T16:05:51Z",
      "updated": "2026-10-17T02:55:38Z",
      "credits": {
        "organizations": []
      },
      "affects": [
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-es"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash.template"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-template"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:gem/lodash-rails"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "GHSA-f23m-r3pf-42rh",
      "references": [
        {
          "id": "CVE-2026-2950",
          "source": {}
        }
      ],
      "ratings": [
        {
          "score": 6.5,
          "severity": "medium",
          "method": "CVSSv3",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:L"
        }
      ],
      "description": "lodash vulnerable to Prototype Pollution via array path bypass in `_.unset` and `_.omit`",
      "detail": "### Impact\n\nLodash versions 4.17.23 and earlier are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the `_.unset` and `_.omit` functions. The fix for [CVE-2025-13465](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg) only guards against string key members, so an attacker can bypass the check by passing array-wrapped path segments. This allows deletion of properties from built-in prototypes such as `Object.prototype`, `Number.prototype`, and `String.prototype`.\n\nThe issue permits deletion of prototype properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis issue is patched in 4.18.0.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNone. Upgrade to the patched version.",
      "advisories": [
        {
          "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-2950"
        }
      ],
      "published": "2026-04-01T23:50:27Z",
      "updated": "2026-10-17T02:56:13Z",
      "credits": {
        "organizations": []
      },
      "affects": [
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-es"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-amd"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash.unset"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc",
      "references": [
        {
          "id": "CVE-2026-4800",
          "source": {}
        }
      ],
      "ratings": [
        {
          "score": 8.1,
          "severity": "high",
          "method": "CVSSv3",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"
        }
      ],
      "description": "lodash vulnerable to Code Injection via `_.template` imports key names",
      "detail": "### Impact\n\nThe fix for [CVE-2021-23337](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm) added validation for the `variable` option in `_.template` but did not apply the same validation to `options.imports` key names. Both paths flow into the same `Function()` constructor sink.\n\nWhen an application passes untrusted input as `options.imports` key names, an attacker can inject default-parameter expressions that execute arbitrary code at template compilation time.\n\nAdditionally, `_.template` uses `assignInWith` to merge imports, which enumerates inherited properties via `for..in`. If `Object.prototype` has been polluted by any other vector, the polluted keys are copied into the imports object and passed to `Function()`.\n\n### Patches\n\nUsers should upgrade to version 4.18.0.\n\nThe fix applies two changes:\n1. Validate `importsKeys` against the existing `reForbiddenIdentifierChars` regex (same check already used for the `variable` option)\n2. Replace `assignInWith` with `assignWith` when merging imports, so only own properties are enumerated\n\n### Workarounds\n\nDo not pass untrusted input as key names in `options.imports`. Only use developer-controlled, static key names.",
      "advisories": [
        {
          "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4800"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm"
        }
      ],
      "published": "2026-04-01T23:51:12Z",
      "updated": "2026-10-17T02:56:15Z",
      "credits": {
        "organizations": []
      },
      "affects": [
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-es"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-amd"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash.template"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "GHSA-xvch-5gv4-984h",
      "references": [
        {
          "id": "CVE-2021-44906",
          "source": {}
        }
      ],
      "ratings": [
        {
          "score": 9.8,
          "severity": "critical",
          "method": "CVSSv3",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Prototype Pollution in minimist",
      "detail": "Minimist prior to 1.2.6 and 0.2.4 is vulnerable to Prototype Pollution via file `index.js`, function `setKey()` (lines 69-95).",
      "advisories": [
        {
          "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-44906"
        }
      ],
      "published": "2022-03-18T00:01:09Z",
      "updated": "2026-03-13T22:11:59Z",
      "credits": {
        "organizations": []
      },
      "affects": [
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/minimist"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg",
      "references": [
        {
          "id": "CVE-2025-13465",
          "source": {}
        }
      ],
      "ratings": [
        {
          "score": 6.5,
          "severity": "medium",
          "method": "CVSSv3",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:L"
        },
        {
          "score": 6.9,
          "severity": "medium",
          "method": "CVSSv4",
          "vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H/E:P"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Lodash has Prototype Pollution Vulnerability in `_.unset` and `_.omit` functions",
      "detail": "### Impact\n\nLodash versions 4.0.0 through 4.17.22 are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the `_.unset` and `_.omit` functions. An attacker can pass crafted paths which cause Lodash to delete methods from global prototypes. \n\nThe issue permits deletion of properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.  \n\n### Patches\n\nThis issue is patched on 4.17.23.",
      "advisories": [
        {
          "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-13465"
        }
      ],
      "published": "2026-01-21T23:01:22Z",
      "updated": "2026-10-17T02:55:54Z",
      "credits": {
        "organizations": []
      },
      "affects": [
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash.unset"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-es"
        },
        {
          "ref": "pkg:npm/lodash-amd"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
